A||N||2||Dick Martin||Where is relay for the air conditioning compressor||||8||
Z||000000||Dick Martin||10-15-2001||03:13 PM||||I can't find it! The two side by side on the front bulkhead seem to control the dash blower motors. Checked the current going to the compressor--there is none, so it must be that relay. ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Denny||10-15-2001||03:19 PM||||On the firewall behind (ahead of) the air cleaner cannister.  Two of them side-by-side.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||10-15-2001||03:43 PM||||Just to expand a little---One of the two relays on the firewall is for the A/C compressor, the other one is the fuel pump relay.  They are identical, so you could swap them out and see if the problem moves with the relay.  You may also want to check the pressure cycling switch up front on the accumulator (large aluminum can).  If it is not closed, you won't have power to the compressor.  An open switch usually indicates a low refrigerant charge.  <P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
